ppe-serving / cpp
Built by Zulfaqar Hafez with Claude Code as the coding agent.

The model
  ppe_yolov8s_320_int8dyn.onnx (not included; downloaded at build time and
  checked against a pinned SHA-256) is a YOLOv8s detector trained by the
  author's teammates in a university course project with Ultralytics YOLOv8.
  Ultralytics YOLOv8 is licensed under AGPL-3.0
  (https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics). The ONNX export and its
  metadata name Ultralytics as the exporter and AGPL-3.0 as its licence.
  The optional fp32 model made by scripts/export_fp32.py comes from the same
  team's published checkpoint (Hugging Face iMaximusiV/yolo-ppe-detector)
  and is not included either.

The dataset and the sample images
  data/samples/*.png are five images from the "Personal Protective
  Equipment" dataset, version 5, Roboflow Universe workspace maxis
  (https://universe.roboflow.com/maxis/personal-protective-equipment-dtt2i-9qixs),
  licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Changes: resized to a long side of 640 px and compressed to WebP for the
  zulfaqarhafez.com demo, then converted losslessly to PNG here.
  data/reference/samples.json records what the model found in them.

